-- **Coco will not stand.** Check both join height and leg spacing. The legs belong on Rnd 4 and Rnd 5; joined any higher, they cannot clear the underside of the body and the belly rests on the table.
-
-- **Coco tips forward or backward.** Most often the front legs are lined up behind the back legs instead of between them - follow the complete Rnd 5 sequence: [sc, inc] x 3, join 3 sc, [sc, inc] x 3, 3 sc, join 3 sc, 3 sc. If still tipping, stuff the lower body more firmly and settle weight back over all four feet.
-
-- **Rocks back, front feet in the air.** All four legs are the same length and they cannot be. Front legs join at Rnd 5 (21 mm up), back at Rnd 4 (17 mm up); work the front legs 9 rounds and the back legs 8.
-
-- **The head flops back.** The Rnd 10 waist is deliberately shallow at 32 stitches - do not decrease it further. A narrow neck cannot hold the head upright.
-
-- **Small hole where a leg meets the body.** Check that the final leg round has six stitches and that each of the three joining sc catches both matching leg stitches plus one body stitch. Do not leave leg stitches unworked or bunched inside.
-
-- **Muzzle looks flat / stuffing shows.** Stuff the muzzle just enough to hold a dome. If stuffing shows through the body, your gauge is too loose - 36 sts should measure 52 mm; crochet tighter or go down a hook size.
